#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:5
#: 205059e6014e4e838826867bbc7a0ebf
msgid "Video Stabilization Using IMU data and Gyroflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:7
#: 4b6573fe4666487f8ee9e9ccfe48cfa7
msgid "ArduPilot provides the means to produce the log data needed for use with `Gyroflow Video Stabilization software <https://gyroflow.xyz/>`_. This software allows the post processing of video taken during a flight with the IMU data logged during the flight to obtain stabilized video."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:12
#: a2d0e375665d4654aa44fdd4087f4a8f
msgid "ArduPilot Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:14
#: 6466af5e4c634cf79560cf5e51ffc5f2
msgid "The following parameters are required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:16
#: 39149d4e5b484cbf91935c38e4077a6f
msgid "The Video Stabilization bit in :ref:`LOG_BITMASK<LOG_BITMASK>` (bit 20 for Copter/Rover, 21 for Plane) must be set (1048576 (Copter/Rover) or 2097152 (Plane) added to present value if not already set) to enable the proper logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:18
#: 31e8692fb4ed4d0d89feb4506c524a50
msgid ":ref:`SCHED_LOOP_RATE<SCHED_LOOP_RATE>` should be set to 300Hz or higher. Planes and Rovers have 50Hz as a default and this should be raised. QuadPlanes and Copters have it already set by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:20
#: eb5c05e58a1e41d1a315a3cb8c7d0228
msgid "Optional: for ease of use, set :ref:`LOG_FILE_DSRMROT<LOG_FILE_DSRMROT>` = 1 to stop logging when disarmed. This allows multiple logs to be generated for multiple flights during a session and makes syncing the logs to the videos easier. Otherwise you would have one big log for multiple flights and videos while powered up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:22
#: ad0e000e172b47ce940d7ddbc21e2317
msgid "Be sure to start the video and arm to start logging at very close to the same time, otherwise you will need to determine the time offset between them and use it for the synchronization dialog's \"Rough gryo offset\" value in Gyroflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:25
#: 4885bced76e8402e8b3e6f2d40a8ac16
msgid "Gyroflow Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:27
#: 262e97ebf1514abbb4631fb15f5c0da9
msgid "Many tutorials exist on YouTube on how to use and adjust Gyroflow, but here is a simplified quickstart for use with ArduPilot, assuming you have installed Gyroflow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:29
#: 2adf3f053d8f431faf71057ce22a2068
msgid "Download the flight log corresponding the video you wish to stabilize. In Mission Planner, under the DataFlash tab, use the .bin to .log button to convert the log .bin file to a .log file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:30
#: 772e4c6bd92c44fe8c0f87e4d11ac16a
msgid "Start Gyroflow program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:31
#: 6a9661117a9b43c880f7603cb0fb6ff9
msgid "Open video file in Gryoflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:32
#: c3929fe630c246d39881c815d1dd2e08
msgid "Select the lens profile for your camera. If it is not listed (unlikely) the there are tutorials  on YouTube as to how to calibrate for your camera."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:33
#: 521cb2c287584c9fab2b653c1744fec9
msgid "Open the .log file you created in the first step above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:34
#: 327a2a6c603b4615a54bcb4bcf8dc166
msgid "Be sure to enter the camera's rotation with respect to the autopilot. Its very common to tilt the camera toward the earth for a better view on a vehicle and this rotation MUST be precisely entered in the \"Rotation\" input boxes in the log data section....typically -10 to -20 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:35
#: 9b140b14c68b46e8bea48679027d5f9b
msgid "use the AutoSync button to synchronize the data and video...the number of points used depends on the video and data, but is easily experimented with. Starting with 4, for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:37
#: 7e1954448d184e7c889baec7d2bc97cc
msgid "You should be able to play a preview of stabilized video at this point and experiment with the other stabilization settings..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gyroflow.rst:39
#: 178c0b9e1724407d940a26ca53d7237e
msgid "if you are getting \"jello\" (CMOS cameras) that you can't remove in the Gyroflow processing, it might be better to hard mount your camera, and maybe get more even more jello in the raw video. The reason is that when soft mounting the camera, it experiences different G-forces than what the autopilot is recording and, therefore Gyroflow, can't compensate. Of course, in some cases the end product can be even worse, so mounting experimentation for your particular setup may be required."
msgstr ""
